IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc29-xxviii-2-peace-810-1.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART XXVII, "Sureties to Keep the Peace": section 810.1 (fear of a sexual offence against a
-- person under 18) and section 810.2 (fear of a serious personal injury offence). Layer 1: the law, objectively. The text is a plain-text
-- rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- The conventions of ccc29-xxviii-0-peace-810.l4 apply unchanged.

§ `Section 810.1 -- Fear of a sexual offence in respect of a person under 18`

-- 810.1(1) Any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under section 151 or 152, subsection 153(1), section 155, subsection 160(2) or (3), section 163.1, 170, 171, 171.1, 172.1 or 172.2, subsection 173(2), section 271, 272, 273 or 279.011, subsection 279.02(2) or 279.03(2), section 280 or 281 or subsection 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2), in respect of one or more persons who are under the age of 18 years, may lay an information before a provincial court judge, whether or not the person or persons in respect of whom it is feared that the offence will be committed are named.
-- src:16991 | Fear of sexual offence
-- src:16992 | 810.1 (1) Any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under section 151 or 152, subsection 153(1), section 155, subsection 160(2) or (3), section 163.1, 170, 171, 171.1, 172.1 or 172.2, subsection 173(2), section 271, 272, 273 or 279.011, subsection 279.02(2) or 279.03(2), section 280 or 281 or subsection 286.1(2), 286.2(2) or 286.3(2), in respect of one or more persons who are under the age of 18 years, may lay an information before a provincial court judge, whether or not the person or persons in respect of whom it is feared that the offence will be committed are named.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(1) (src:16991-16992)
GIVEN `the feared offence is an offence under this provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(1) the feared offence is one of those listed` MEANS
    IF `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 151
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 152
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 155
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 163.1
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 170
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 171
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 171.1
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 172.1
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 172.2
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 271
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 272
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 273
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 279.011
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 280
       OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 281
       OR (`the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 153 AND `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
       OR (`the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 160 AND (`the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)" OR `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)"))
       OR (`the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 173 AND `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")
       OR (`the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 279.02 AND `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")
       OR (`the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 279.03 AND `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")
       OR (`the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 286.1 AND `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")
       OR (`the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 286.2 AND `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")
       OR (`the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `section` EQUALS 286.3 AND `the feared offence is an offence under this provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "an offence under section 151 or 152, subsection 153(1), section 155, ..."

@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(1) (src:16991-16992)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; relative-clause gate "Any person who fears on reasonable grounds" (fork F-810.1-1)
GIVEN `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the feared offence is one of those listed, by s 810.1(1) the feared offence is one of those listed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the feared offence is in respect of one or more persons who are under the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` MEANS
    IF `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit the offence`
       AND `the feared offence is one of those listed, by s 810.1(1) the feared offence is one of those listed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the feared offence is in respect of one or more persons who are under the age of 18 years`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under ... in respect of one or more persons who are under the age of 18 years"

-- "whether or not the person or persons in respect of whom it is feared that the offence will be committed are named": naming them is not a condition, so the function above takes no input for it (fork F-810.1-1b).

-- 810.1(2) A provincial court judge who receives an information under subsection (1) may cause the parties to appear before a provincial court judge.
-- src:16993 | Appearances
-- src:16994 | (2) A provincial court judge who receives an information under subsection (1) may cause the parties to appear before a provincial court judge.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(2) (src:16993-16994)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside the scope
GIVEN `the provincial court judge receives an information under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(2) the provincial court judge may cause the parties to appear` MEANS
    IF `the provincial court judge receives an information under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A provincial court judge who receives an information under subsection (1)"

-- 810.1(3) If the provincial court judge before whom the parties appear is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear, the judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance to keep the peace and be of good behaviour for a period that does not exceed 12 months.
-- src:16996 | (3) If the provincial court judge before whom the parties appear is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear, the judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance to keep the peace and be of good behaviour for a period that does not exceed 12 months.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3) (src:16996)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "If ... is satisfied" (fork F-810.1-3)
GIVEN `the provincial court judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(3) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the provincial court judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the provincial court judge before whom the parties appear is satisfied by the evidence adduced"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3) (src:16996)
GIVEN `the period of the recognizance in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(3) the period of the recognizance does not exceed 12 months` MEANS
    IF `the period of the recognizance in months` AT MOST 12
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period that does not exceed 12 months"

-- 810.1(3.01) However, if the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously of a sexual offence in respect of a person who is under the age of 18 years, the judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a period of not more than two years.
-- src:16997 | Duration extended
-- src:16998 | (3.01) However, if the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously of a sexual offence in respect of a person who is under the age of 18 years, the judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a period of not more than two years.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.01) (src:16997-16998)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "if the provincial court judge is also satisfied" (fork F-810.1-3.01)
GIVEN `the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously of a sexual offence in respect of a person who is under the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(3.01) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a longer period` MEANS
    IF `the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously of a sexual offence in respect of a person who is under the age of 18 years`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously of a sexual offence"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.01) (src:16997-16998)
GIVEN `the period of the recognizance in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(3.01) the longer period of the recognizance is not more than two years` MEANS
    IF `the period of the recognizance in months` AT MOST 24
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than two years"

-- 810.1(3.02) The provincial court judge may add any reasonable conditions ... including conditions that (a) prohibit ... any contact ... with a person under the age of 18 years, unless ... under the supervision of a person whom the judge considers appropriate; (a.1) prohibit ... using the Internet or other digital network, unless ... in accordance with conditions set by the judge; (b) prohibit ... attending a public park or public swimming area where persons under the age of 18 years are present ...; (b.1) prohibit ... communicating ... with any person identified in the recognizance, or ... going to any place specified ...; (c) require ... a treatment program; (d) ... an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request; (e) ... a specified geographic area ...; (f) ... place of residence at specified times; (g) ... abstain from the consumption of drugs ...; (h) ... a sample ... on demand ...; or (i) ... a sample ... at regular intervals ... Form 51.
-- src:16999 | Conditions in recognizance
-- src:17000 | (3.02) The provincial court judge may add any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant, including conditions that
-- src:17001 | (a) prohibit the defendant from having any contact — including communicating by any means — with a person under the age of 18 years, unless the defendant does so under the supervision of a person whom the judge considers appropriate;
-- src:17002 | (a.1) prohibit the defendant from using the Internet or other digital network, unless the defendant does so in accordance with conditions set by the judge;
-- src:17003 | (b) prohibit the defendant from attending a public park or public swimming area where persons under the age of 18 years are present or can reasonably be expected to be present, or a daycare centre, schoolground or playground;
-- src:17004 | (b.1) prohibit the defendant from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any person identified in the recognizance, or refrain from going to any place specified in the recognizance, except in accordance with the conditions specified in the recognizance that the judge considers necessary;
-- src:17005 | (c) require the defendant to participate in a treatment program;
-- src:17006 | (d) require the defendant to wear an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request;
-- src:17007 | (e) require the defendant to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the provincial court judge;
-- src:17008 | (f) require the defendant to return to and remain at his or her place of residence at specified times;
-- src:17009 | (g) require the defendant to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:17010 | (h) require the defendant to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation on the demand of a peace officer, a probation officer or someone designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(a) to make a demand, at the place and time and on the day specified by the person making the demand, if that person has reasonable grounds to believe that the defendant has breached a condition of the recognizance that requires them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance; or
-- src:17011 | (i) require the defendant to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals that are specified, in a notice in Form 51 served on the defendant, by a probation officer or a person designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(b) to specify them, if a condition of the recognizance requires the defendant to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.02) to s 810.1(3.02)(i) (src:16999-17011)
DECLARE `s 810.1(3.02) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.1(3.02)(a) to prohibit any contact with a person under the age of 18 years, unless under the supervision of a person whom the judge considers appropriate`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(a.1) to prohibit the use of the Internet or other digital network, unless in accordance with conditions set by the judge`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(b) to prohibit attending a public park or public swimming area where persons under 18 are present or a daycare centre, schoolground or playground`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(b.1) to prohibit communicating with any person identified in the recognizance, or going to any place specified in it`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(c) to require the defendant to participate in a treatment program`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(d) to require the defendant to wear an electronic monitoring device`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(e) to require the defendant to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the provincial court judge`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(f) to require the defendant to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(g) to require the defendant to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(h) to require the defendant to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand`
    `s 810.1(3.02)(i) to require the defendant to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51`
    `s 810.1(3.02) another reasonable condition`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.02) (src:16999-17000)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside "any reasonable conditions that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant"
GIVEN condition IS A `s 810.1(3.02) condition`
      `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers the condition desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General makes the request for an electronic monitoring device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(3.02) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the condition is reasonable` AND `the judge considers the condition desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant`
    THEN CONSIDER condition
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(a) to prohibit any contact with a person under the age of 18 years, unless under the supervision of a person whom the judge considers appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(a.1) to prohibit the use of the Internet or other digital network, unless in accordance with conditions set by the judge` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(b) to prohibit attending a public park or public swimming area where persons under 18 are present or a daycare centre, schoolground or playground` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(b.1) to prohibit communicating with any person identified in the recognizance, or going to any place specified in it` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(c) to require the defendant to participate in a treatment program` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(d) to require the defendant to wear an electronic monitoring device` THEN IF `the Attorney General makes the request for an electronic monitoring device` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Attorney General makes the request"
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(e) to require the defendant to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the provincial court judge` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(f) to require the defendant to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(g) to require the defendant to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(h) to require the defendant to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02)(i) to require the defendant to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.1(3.02) another reasonable condition` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant"

-- 810.1(3.03) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable ... to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm ... If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
-- src:17012 | Conditions — firearms
-- src:17013 | (3.03) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the defendant’s safety or that of any other person, to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things. If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.03) (src:17012-17013)
GIVEN `the information was laid under section 810.1 and the defendant is before the provincial court judge for an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(3.03) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` MEANS
    IF `the information was laid under section 810.1 and the defendant is before the provincial court judge for an order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provincial court judge shall consider" in proceedings under this section

@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.03) (src:17012-17013)
GIVEN `the judge decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(3.03) the provincial court judge is required to add the firearms condition and specify the period during which it applies` MEANS
    IF `the judge decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so"

DECLARE `s 810.1 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.1(3.03) consider the firearms condition`
    `s 810.1(3.03) add the firearms condition and specify the period`
    `s 810.1(3.04) specify how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered`
    `s 810.1(3.05) consider the reporting condition`
    `s 810.1(3.05) add the reporting condition`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.03) (src:17012-17013)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.1 action`
`s 810.1(3.03) the judge is to consider the firearms condition` MEANS
    PARTY `a provincial court judge`
    MUST `s 810.1(3.03) consider the firearms condition`
    HENCE `s 810.1(3.03) the judge is to add the firearms condition if it is desirable`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.03) (src:17012-17013)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.1 action`
`s 810.1(3.03) the judge is to add the firearms condition if it is desirable` MEANS
    PARTY `a provincial court judge`
    MUST `s 810.1(3.03) add the firearms condition and specify the period`

-- 810.1(3.04) If the provincial court judge adds a condition described in subsection (3.03) to a recognizance, the judge shall specify in the recognizance how the things ... should be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with and how the authorizations, licences and registration certificates ... should be surrendered.
