-- 810.1(3.1) The provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison for a term not exceeding twelve months if the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance.
-- src:17018 | Refusal to enter into recognizance
-- src:17019 | (3.1) The provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison for a term not exceeding twelve months if the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.1) (src:17018-17019)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "if the defendant fails or refuses" (fork F-810.1-3.1)
GIVEN `the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(3.1) the provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison` MEANS
    IF `the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(3.1) (src:17018-17019)
GIVEN `the term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(3.1) the term of imprisonment does not exceed twelve months` MEANS
    IF `the term of imprisonment in months` AT MOST 12
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a term not exceeding twelve months"

-- 810.1(4) A provincial court judge may, on application of the informant or the defendant, vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance.
-- src:17020 | Judge may vary recognizance
-- src:17021 | (4) A provincial court judge may, on application of the informant or the defendant, vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.1(4) (src:17020-17021)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-810.1-4); answers JUST FALSE when neither the informant nor the defendant applies
GIVEN `the informant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(4) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the informant applies` OR `the defendant applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the informant or the defendant"

