GIVEN `the recognizance is made under section 810.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.1(5) subsections 810(4) and (5) apply to the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the recognizance is made under section 810.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to recognizances made under this section"

§ `Section 810.2 -- Fear of a serious personal injury offence`

-- 810.2(1) Any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit a serious personal injury offence, as that expression is defined in section 752, may, with the consent of the Attorney General, lay an information before a provincial court judge, whether or not the person or persons in respect of whom it is feared that the offence will be committed are named.
-- src:17024 | Where fear of serious personal injury offence
-- src:17025 | 810.2 (1) Any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit a serious personal injury offence, as that expression is defined in section 752, may, with the consent of the Attorney General, lay an information before a provincial court judge, whether or not the person or persons in respect of whom it is feared that the offence will be committed are named.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(1) (src:17024-17025)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; relative-clause gate and "with the consent of the Attorney General" (fork F-810.2-1)
GIVEN `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit a serious personal injury offence, as that expression is defined in section 752` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` MEANS
    IF `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit a serious personal injury offence, as that expression is defined in section 752` AND `the Attorney General consents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who fears on reasonable grounds ... may, with the consent of the Attorney General, lay an information"

-- 810.2(2) A provincial court judge who receives an information under subsection (1) may cause the parties to appear before a provincial court judge.
-- src:17026 | Appearances
-- src:17027 | (2) A provincial court judge who receives an information under subsection (1) may cause the parties to appear before a provincial court judge.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(2) (src:17026-17027)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside the scope
GIVEN `the provincial court judge receives an information under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(2) the provincial court judge may cause the parties to appear` MEANS
    IF `the provincial court judge receives an information under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A provincial court judge who receives an information under subsection (1)"

-- 810.2(3) If the provincial court judge before whom the parties appear is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear, the judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance to keep the peace and be of good behaviour for a period that does not exceed 12 months.
-- src:17029 | (3) If the provincial court judge before whom the parties appear is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear, the judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance to keep the peace and be of good behaviour for a period that does not exceed 12 months.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(3) (src:17029)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "If ... is satisfied" (fork F-810.2-3)
GIVEN `the provincial court judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(3) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the provincial court judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the provincial court judge before whom the parties appear is satisfied by the evidence adduced"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(3) (src:17029)
GIVEN `the period of the recognizance in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(3) the period of the recognizance does not exceed 12 months` MEANS
    IF `the period of the recognizance in months` AT MOST 12
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period that does not exceed 12 months"

-- 810.2(3.1) However, if the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously of an offence referred to in subsection (1), the judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a period that does not exceed two years.
-- src:17030 | Duration extended
-- src:17031 | (3.1) However, if the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously of an offence referred to in subsection (1), the judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a period that does not exceed two years.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(3.1) (src:17030-17031)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "if the provincial court judge is also satisfied" (fork F-810.2-3.1)
GIVEN `the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously of an offence referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(3.1) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into the recognizance for a longer period` MEANS
    IF `the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously of an offence referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the provincial court judge is also satisfied that the defendant was convicted previously"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(3.1) (src:17030-17031)
GIVEN `the period of the recognizance in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(3.1) the longer period of the recognizance does not exceed two years` MEANS
    IF `the period of the recognizance in months` AT MOST 24
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period that does not exceed two years"

-- 810.2(4) The provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison for a term not exceeding twelve months if the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance.
-- src:17032 | Refusal to enter into recognizance
-- src:17033 | (4) The provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison for a term not exceeding twelve months if the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(4) (src:17032-17033)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "if the defendant fails or refuses" (fork F-810.2-4)
GIVEN `the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(4) the provincial court judge may commit the defendant to prison` MEANS
    IF `the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the defendant fails or refuses to enter into the recognizance"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(4) (src:17032-17033)
GIVEN `the term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(4) the term of imprisonment does not exceed twelve months` MEANS
    IF `the term of imprisonment in months` AT MOST 12
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a term not exceeding twelve months"

-- 810.2(4.1) The provincial court judge may add any reasonable conditions ... including conditions that require the defendant (a) to participate in a treatment program; (b) to wear an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request; (c) to remain within a specified geographic area ...; (d) to return to and remain at his or her place of residence at specified times; (e) to abstain from the consumption of drugs ...; (f) to provide ... a sample ... on demand ...; or (g) to provide ... a sample ... at regular intervals ... Form 51.
-- src:17034 | Conditions in recognizance
-- src:17035 | (4.1) The provincial court judge may add any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant, including conditions that require the defendant
-- src:17036 | (a) to participate in a treatment program;
-- src:17037 | (b) to wear an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request;
-- src:17038 | (c) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the provincial court judge;
-- src:17039 | (d) to return to and remain at his or her place of residence at specified times;
-- src:17040 | (e) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:17041 | (f) to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation on the demand of a peace officer, a probation officer or someone designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(a) to make a demand, at the place and time and on the day specified by the person making the demand, if that person has reasonable grounds to believe that the defendant has breached a condition of the recognizance that requires them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance; or
-- src:17042 | (g) to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals that are specified, in a notice in Form 51 served on the defendant, by a probation officer or a person designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(b) to specify them, if a condition of the recognizance requires the defendant to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(4.1) to s 810.2(4.1)(g) (src:17034-17042)
DECLARE `s 810.2(4.1) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.2(4.1)(a) to participate in a treatment program`
    `s 810.2(4.1)(b) to wear an electronic monitoring device`
    `s 810.2(4.1)(c) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the provincial court judge`
    `s 810.2(4.1)(d) to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times`
    `s 810.2(4.1)(e) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance`
    `s 810.2(4.1)(f) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand`
    `s 810.2(4.1)(g) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51`
    `s 810.2(4.1) another reasonable condition`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(4.1) (src:17034-17035)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside "any reasonable conditions that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant"
GIVEN condition IS A `s 810.2(4.1) condition`
      `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers the condition desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General makes the request for an electronic monitoring device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(4.1) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the condition is reasonable` AND `the judge considers the condition desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant`
    THEN CONSIDER condition
         WHEN `s 810.2(4.1)(a) to participate in a treatment program` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.2(4.1)(b) to wear an electronic monitoring device` THEN IF `the Attorney General makes the request for an electronic monitoring device` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Attorney General makes the request"
         WHEN `s 810.2(4.1)(c) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the provincial court judge` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.2(4.1)(d) to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.2(4.1)(e) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.2(4.1)(f) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.2(4.1)(g) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.2(4.1) another reasonable condition` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant"

-- 810.2(5) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable ... to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm ... If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
-- src:17043 | Conditions — firearms
-- src:17044 | (5) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the defendant’s safety or that of any other person, to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things. If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(5) (src:17043-17044)
GIVEN `the information was laid under section 810.2 and the defendant is before the provincial court judge for an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(5) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` MEANS
    IF `the information was laid under section 810.2 and the defendant is before the provincial court judge for an order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provincial court judge shall consider" in proceedings under this section

@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(5) (src:17043-17044)
GIVEN `the judge decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(5) the provincial court judge is required to add the firearms condition and specify the period during which it applies` MEANS
    IF `the judge decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so"

DECLARE `s 810.2 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.2(5) consider the firearms condition`
    `s 810.2(5) add the firearms condition and specify the period`
    `s 810.2(5.1) specify how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered`
    `s 810.2(5.2) include a statement of reasons in the record`
    `s 810.2(6) consider the reporting condition`
    `s 810.2(6) add the reporting condition`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(5) (src:17043-17044)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.2 action`
`s 810.2(5) the judge is to consider the firearms condition` MEANS
    PARTY `a provincial court judge`
    MUST `s 810.2(5) consider the firearms condition`
    HENCE `s 810.2(5) the judge is to add the firearms condition if it is desirable`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(5) (src:17043-17044)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.2 action`
`s 810.2(5) the judge is to add the firearms condition if it is desirable` MEANS
    PARTY `a provincial court judge`
    MUST `s 810.2(5) add the firearms condition and specify the period`

-- 810.2(5.1) If the provincial court judge adds a condition described in subsection (5) to a recognizance, the judge shall specify in the recognizance how the things ... should be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with and how the authorizations, licences and registration certificates ... should be surrendered.
-- src:17045 | Surrender, etc.
-- src:17046 | (5.1) If the provincial court judge adds a condition described in subsection (5) to a recognizance, the judge shall specify in the recognizance how the things referred to in that subsection that are in the defendant’s possession should be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with and how the authorizations, licences and registration certificates that are held by the defendant should be surrendered.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(5.1) (src:17045-17046)
GIVEN `the judge adds a condition described in subsection (5) to a recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
