-- 810.2(7) A provincial court judge may, on application of the informant, of the Attorney General or of the defendant, vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance.
-- src:17051 | Variance of conditions
-- src:17052 | (7) A provincial court judge may, on application of the informant, of the Attorney General or of the defendant, vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.2(7) (src:17051-17052)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-810.2-7); answers JUST FALSE when no one of the three applies
GIVEN `the informant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.2(7) the provincial court judge may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the informant applies` OR `the Attorney General applies` OR `the defendant applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the informant, of the Attorney General or of the defendant"

